---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { SAWA_RATTI_TABLE } from '../../utils/converter';

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BlogPosting',
  headline: 'Vedic Sawa Ratti Guide: Why 5.25, 6.25, and 7.25 Ratti are Auspicious (and Paune Warnings)',
  description: 'Discover the ancient Vedic Jyotish science behind Sawa (+0.25) and Paune (-0.25) gemstone weights, planetary ruling connections, and body weight dosage rules.',
  author: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Ratti to Carat Research Team',
    url: 'https://rattitocarat.com'
  },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Ratti to Carat',
    logo: {
      '@type': 'ImageObject',
      url: 'https://rattitocarat.com/favicon.svg'
    }
  },
  datePublished: '2025-01-20',
  dateModified: '2025-01-20',
  image: 'https://rattitocarat.com/og-image.png',
  mainEntityOfPage: {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': 'https://rattitocarat.com/blog/sawa-ratti-astrological-rules'
  }
};
---

<Layout
  title="Vedic Sawa Ratti Guide: Why 5.25 & 7.25 are Auspicious | Ratti to Carat"
  description="Comprehensive Jyotish guide explaining why astrologers prescribe Sawa (+0.25) weights like 5.25 and 7.25 Ratti, why Paune (-0.25) must be avoided, and body weight dosage."
  canonicalUrl="https://rattitocarat.com/blog/sawa-ratti-astrological-rules"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} slot="head" />

  <Navbar />

  <main class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 space-y-10">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-slate-500 font-mono">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-amber-700 transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-amber-700 transition-colors">Blog</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-slate-800 font-semibold truncate">Vedic Sawa Ratti Guide</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Article Header -->
    <header class="space-y-4 text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-50 text-amber-800 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-amber-200">
          Vedic Astrology & Jyotish
        </span>
        <span class="text-slate-400">•</span>
        <span class="text-slate-500 font-mono">7 Min Read</span>
        <span class="text-slate-400">•</span>
        <span class="text-slate-500 font-mono">Updated Jan 2025</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 font-display leading-tight">
        Vedic Sawa Ratti Guide: Why 5.25, 6.25, and 7.25 Ratti are Auspicious
      </h1>

      <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Understanding the sacred numerology of Sapada (+0.25) growth fractions, why Paune (-0.25) weights are strictly forbidden, and how to calibrate gemstone mass to your body weight.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Key Takeaway Box -->
    <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-3xl bg-amber-50/70 border border-amber-200/80 space-y-2 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold text-amber-900 uppercase tracking-wide">
        <span>🧘 Core Astrological Principles</span>
      </div>
      <ul class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside">
        <li><strong>Sawa (Sapada / +0.25):</strong> Represents surplus, overflow, and progressive evolution. Highly recommended by astrologers.</li>
        <li><strong>Paune (Padona / -0.25 / 0.75):</strong> Represents deficit, deficiency, and struggle. Classical texts advise never wearing Paune stones.</li>
        <li><strong>Body Weight Formula:</strong> Minimum Ratti = <code>Body Weight in kg ÷ 10 to 12</code> (e.g. 65 kg requires ~5.25 to 6.25 Ratti).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Article Body -->
    <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-slate-700 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed space-y-8">
      
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display">
          1. The Sanskrit Roots: Sapada (सपाद) vs Padona (पदों)
        </h2>
        <p>
          In classical Vedic mathematics and Jyotish Shastra, fractions carry energetic resonance. When an astrologer asks a seeker to wear <strong>"Sawa Paanch Ratti" (5.25 Rt)</strong> or <strong>"Sawa Saat Ratti" (7.25 Rt)</strong>, they are invoking the Sanskrit concept of <em>Sapada</em> (सपाद — literally "with a quarter added").
        </p>
        <p>
          In traditional Indian ceremonies, shagun gifts are invariably presented as ₹101, ₹501, or 1.25 units rather than whole numbers. The additional quarter signifies that your destiny is not bounded or static; it is expanding and open to higher divine blessings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display">
          2. The Warning: Why "Paune" (0.75) Weights Must Be Avoided
        </h2>
        <p>
          Conversely, fractional weights ending in <strong>0.75</strong> (such as 4.75, 5.75, or 6.75 Ratti) are known in Hindi as <em>Paune</em> (from the Sanskrit <em>Padona</em> — meaning "lacking one quarter").
        </p>
        <p>
          In Vedic philosophy, an incomplete unit attracts incompleteness in the wearer's life. If you wear a 5.75 Ratti stone:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li>It energetically pulls toward a deficit, dampening planetary benefits.</li>
          <li>Astrologers consistently advise rounding up to the nearest auspicious Sawa weight (for example, choosing <strong>6.25 Ratti</strong> instead of 5.75 Ratti).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display">
          3. Sawa Ratti to Carat Master Reference Chart
        </h2>
        <p>
          When you purchase an auspicious Sawa stone, the lab certificate will list the weight in <strong>Carats</strong>. Use this reference matrix based on certified 0.9100 Pakka Ratti:
        </p>

        <!-- Sawa Reference Table -->
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 my-4">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono border-collapse">
            <thead class="bg-slate-50 text-slate-700 uppercase font-semibold border-b border-slate-200">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3">Sawa Fraction</th>
                <th class="p-3">Weight (Ratti)</th>
                <th class="p-3">Carats (0.91 Pakka)</th>
                <th class="p-3">Ruling Planet</th>
                <th class="p-3">Associated Gem</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 bg-white">
              {SAWA_RATTI_TABLE.slice(0, 7).map((row) => (
                <tr class="hover:bg-amber-50/40 transition-colors">
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans font-bold text-amber-800">✨ {row.name} ({row.hindiName})</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-900">{row.ratti.toFixed(2)} Rt</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-900">{row.carat.toFixed(2)} Ct</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans text-slate-700">{row.planet}</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans text-amber-700 font-semibold">{row.gem}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display">
          4. How to Calculate Gemstone Weight by Body Weight
        </h2>
        <p>
          A gemstone acts as an optical prism channeling planetary cosmic rays directly into the physical body. A child weighing 30 kg does not require the same energetic dosage as an adult weighing 85 kg.
        </p>
        <p>
          The universal classical guideline followed across Indian Vedic schools:
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 space-y-1">
          <div>Minimum Ratti = Body Weight in kg ÷ 12</div>
          <div>Optimal Ratti = Body Weight in kg ÷ 10</div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
          Example: For an individual weighing <strong>65 kg</strong>, the baseline dosage is <code>65 ÷ 12 = 5.41 Rt</code>, making <strong>5.25 Ratti (Sawa Paanch)</strong> or <strong>6.25 Ratti (Sawa Chhe)</strong> the ideal prescribed window.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Bottom Interactive CTA -->
      <section class="p-6 rounded-2xl atelier-card-elevated border border-amber-300/80 bg-amber-50/50 space-y-3 text-center my-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 font-display">
          Calculate Your Exact Body Weight Dosage
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 max-w-md mx-auto">
          Try our interactive Body Weight Dosage Calculator to calculate your personalized Sawa Ratti prescription with a single slider movement.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <a
            href="/body-weight-calculator"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-800 text-white font-bold text-xs shadow-sm transition-all hover:scale-105"
          >
            <span>Launch Body Weight Tool →</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
